# Calling the bedrock-api proxy — {{OWNER}}

The proxy accepts standard [AWS Bedrock Converse](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/APIReference/API_runtime_Converse.html)
and InvokeModel request bodies. Authentication is a bearer token in the
`Authorization` header — no SigV4 signing required.

**Streaming is not supported in v1.**

Your token is provisioned with a **${{BUDGET_USD}}/month USD budget**. Once exhausted,
requests return `429 MONTHLY_BUDGET_EXCEEDED` until the next billing period.

---

## Your credentials

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| Owner | `{{OWNER}}` |
| Token ID | `{{TOKEN_ID}}` |
| Bearer token | `{{BEARER_TOKEN}}` |
| API URL | `{{API_URL}}` |
| Monthly budget | ${{BUDGET_USD}} |
| Per-second rate (RPS) | {{RPS}} |
| Monthly request quota | {{MONTHLY_REQUESTS}} |
| Max input tokens / request | {{MAX_INPUT_TOKENS}} |
| Max output tokens / request | {{MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS}} |
| Allowed models | {{ALLOWED_MODELS}} |

Treat the bearer token like a password. It is shown once at issue time and
cannot be recovered later.

---

## Endpoint format

```
POST {API_URL}/model/{url-encoded-model-id}/converse
POST {API_URL}/model/{url-encoded-model-id}/invoke
```

Model IDs contain colons (`:`), which must be percent-encoded as `%3A`:

| Model | Path segment |
|---|---|
| `us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6` | `us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6` |
| `us.anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1:0` | `us.anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1%3A0` |

---

## curl

```bash
API_URL="{{API_URL}}"
TOKEN="{{BEARER_TOKEN}}"
MODEL="us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6"

curl -s -X POST "${API_URL}/model/${MODEL}/converse" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer ${TOKEN}" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "messages": [
      {"role": "user", "content": [{"text": "Hello!"}]}
    ]
  }' | jq .
```

---

## Python — httpx

```python
from urllib.parse import quote
import httpx

API_URL = "{{API_URL}}"
TOKEN = "{{BEARER_TOKEN}}"
MODEL_ID = "us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6"

url = f"{API_URL}/model/{quote(MODEL_ID, safe='')}/converse"

response = httpx.post(
    url,
    headers={"Authorization": f"Bearer {TOKEN}"},
    json={
        "messages": [
            {"role": "user", "content": [{"text": "Hello!"}]}
        ]
    },
    timeout=30.0,
)
response.raise_for_status()
print(response.json()["output"]["message"]["content"][0]["text"])
```

